sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant BR as Browser
    participant KF as kubectl port-forward<br/>(127.0.0.1:3000)
    participant API as kube-apiserver :6443
    participant KL as kubelet (docker-desktop)
    participant NX as frontend pod<br/>nginx :80
    participant CD as CoreDNS :53
    participant KP as kube-proxy<br/>(iptables/IPVS DNAT)
    participant BE as backend pod<br/>Spring Boot :8080
    participant PG as postgres-0 pod<br/>PostgreSQL :5432

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
    Note over BR,KF: TCP 1 — plain HTTP on loopback (no TLS)
    BR->>KF: GET http://localhost:3000/
    Note over KF,API: TCP 2 — HTTPS + SPDY stream (TLS, kubeconfig client cert)
    KF->>API: POST /api/v1/namespaces/financialgps/pods/frontend-xxx/portforward
    API->>KL: relay stream
    KL->>NX: forward into pod netns (10.1.0.112:80)
    NX-->>BR: 200 OK: index.html + JS/CSS (reverse path)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 230)
    BR->>KF: GET /api/v1/account/me (with SESSION cookie)
    KF->>API: (same tunnel)
    API->>KL: relay
    KL->>NX: deliver request
    NX->>CD: resolve "backend" (UDP 53)
    CD-->>NX: ClusterIP 10.96.x.x
    Note over NX,BE: TCP 3 — new connection to ClusterIP:8080
    NX->>KP: SYN to 10.96.x.x:8080
    KP->>BE: DNAT to 10.1.0.110 (per-connection LB)
    BE->>CD: resolve "postgres" (headless Service)
    CD-->>BE: pod IP 10.1.0.114
    Note over BE,PG: TCP 4 — JDBC to postgres:5432 (StatefulSet, stable pod IP)
    BE->>PG: SELECT on SPRING_SESSION, then accounts
    PG-->>BE: rows
    BE-->>NX: 200 account JSON (401 if session unknown/expired)
    NX-->>BR: response via reverse tunnel
    end
